INT. SAFE HOUSE - BASEMENT - NIGHT

A bare concrete room. A table, six folding chairs, a bank of dead monitors. A phone sits in the center on speaker.

AGENT NADEZHDA KOVACS, 40s, at the head. LUCIEN BRASSARD, 50s, beside her. Across, three more: TAVITA SEFO, 30s; MARGOT FENWICK, 60s; and a nervous young man in a stolen hoodie, UNKNOWN MALE, 20s, who has not given a name.

                    HANDLER (V.O.)
(over speaker)
Status.

                    NADEZHDA
All present. The package is secure.

                    HANDLER (V.O.)
(over speaker)
Is he talking?

                    NADEZHDA
Not yet.

                    HANDLER (V.O.)
(over speaker)
Make him.

She mutes the line. Turns to the young man.

                    NADEZHDA (CONT'D)
They won't wait much longer. You understand that.

                    UNKNOWN MALE
I understand I didn't do anything.

                    LUCIEN
Everyone in this room did something.

                    UNKNOWN MALE
I drove a car.

                    MARGOT
To where?

                    UNKNOWN MALE
A warehouse. Pier nine. I didn't ask what was inside.

                    TAVITA
Who told you to drive?

                    UNKNOWN MALE
A guy. Short. Gold tooth.

                    NADEZHDA
His name?

                    UNKNOWN MALE
Dmitri. Everybody called him Dmitri.

                    LUCIEN
Dmitri Volkov.

                    UNKNOWN MALE
That's him.

Lucien and Nadezhda exchange a look. Margot rises and pours water into a paper cup, sets it in front of the boy.

                    MARGOT
Drink.

                    TAVITA
Tell us about the pier.

                    UNKNOWN MALE
There were crates. Eight. Stenciled with a bird.

                    NADEZHDA
What kind of bird?

                    UNKNOWN MALE
A heron. No. A crane.

                    LUCIEN
Crane.

                    UNKNOWN MALE
And there was a woman.

                    NADEZHDA
Describe her.

                    UNKNOWN MALE
Red coat. She never spoke. Dmitri was scared of her.

The phone crackles. Nadezhda unmutes.

                    HANDLER (V.O.)
(over speaker)
Kovacs. We have a name.

                    NADEZHDA
Go ahead.

                    HANDLER (V.O.)
(over speaker)
The woman in the red coat. Margot Fenwick.

Silence. Everyone turns.

Margot sets down the pitcher. Folds her hands. Smiles, almost tenderly.

                    MARGOT
Oh, dear.
